# Git push + GitHub (Cursor / PowerShell)

Before `git push`, if you see **403 Permission denied** on `https://github.com/...`:

1. Run `gh auth status`. If **Active account** is **`GITHUB_TOKEN`**, that env PAT is often **read-only** or missing `repo` write — it overrides the keyring token.
2. Fix session: `Remove-Item Env:GITHUB_TOKEN -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue`, then `gh auth switch --hostname github.com --user <github-user-with-repo-write>`.
3. Run `gh auth setup-git` so Git uses the same credentials as `gh` for `github.com`.
4. Use **HTTPS** `origin` (`https://github.com/OWNER/REPO.git`) when relying on `gh` helper; SSH needs a working `ssh-agent` + keys (Windows `ssh-agent` service must not be **Disabled** if you use service-based agent).
5. Never paste tokens in chat.
